{"event_type":"review","id":"1c998e7d8d19e371a6d765a66e4b0caff3f124593dd50494cdb29328a4189d52","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T22:23:25Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0107af7c1a9665f9231adca0a4fda47a865ca13a966aa0f72055ab7e379de03c","sha256":"0107af7c1a9665f9231adca0a4fda47a865ca13a966aa0f72055ab7e379de03c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/07b46dd4852983c4dc31f47c93ca7ad62465a0e9bc736570777de6a4d5281a65","sha256":"07b46dd4852983c4dc31f47c93ca7ad62465a0e9bc736570777de6a4d5281a65"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c60fc448bb88b527069a63aa82812320ff96da54ea72a22f5e5109e50ac0b785","sha256":"c60fc448bb88b527069a63aa82812320ff96da54ea72a22f5e5109e50ac0b785"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4eaa53d794a1ac55a68dc739f3a342cf7a9bbfee75d47cb4a4a0c47c59a51d0b","sha256":"4eaa53d794a1ac55a68dc739f3a342cf7a9bbfee75d47cb4a4a0c47c59a51d0b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9b02d59114241c23a87587659f66532d615c4d0cd3e1644036c9b5a2d45364c6","sha256":"9b02d59114241c23a87587659f66532d615c4d0cd3e1644036c9b5a2d45364c6"}],"attempt_id":"548e6c6410a06637861563a2d6eca21316446eb48bf232e4752dde224591095a:0:1","base":"3fbb9f320dc5abbea1b34140a0d62d1da20271b5","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"17e075dd429f2875a912a0a6ee27271576d558a6","body":"**Decode Git-quoted paths before applying scan rules.**\n\nAt `authorSnapshotInstall.ts:313-316`, a quoted path retains its quotes and escapes. Git quotes non-ASCII filenames by default. Thus, deletion of `secrét.env` does not match a loaded path rule such as `\\.env$`. ([git-scm.com](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config/2.49.0))\n\nThe later entry scan excludes deletions at Line 378. If gitleaks is absent, a project-rule match in the removed content can pass installation.\n\nDecode Git path quoting before matching rules. Refuse paths that cannot be decoded safely.","id":"cecaee8a0b19e7e532b02601ef490637834dbbb639d998f1cfd39b5e78bdad42","intervals":[[313,316]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/authorSnapshotInstall.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Decode Git-quoted paths before applying scan rules."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"cd13cdf1a7ac37ab98bf40add57b7cabb038ee33","body":"**Preserve filename bytes before decoding.**\n\nAt `reviewVerify.ts:109`, replacement decoding merges distinct Git paths. Names with bytes `ff2e7473` and `efbfbd2e7473` both become `�.ts`. `ledgerPath` accepts that name, so Line 125 overwrites one entry instead of preserving both. Replacement decoding cannot support the documented byte-hex fallback. ([encoding.spec.whatwg.org](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/))\n\nSplit the output into byte records first. Decode each filename strictly, and build the fallback from its original bytes.","id":"c9f6f1907c3eb936a826190b755cc2e4323bc057d49f60f842efb770e67af447","intervals":[[109,109]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/reviewVerify.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve filename bytes before decoding."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"97917f96b38ccc9113624d32ccd4108ad49a52c2","body":"**Preserve intervals for quoted Git pathnames.**\n\nFor a regular UTF8 file named `src/a\"b.ts`, `ledgerPath` and inventory accept the path. Git quotes the patch pathname even when `core.quotePath=false`. ([git-scm.com](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config/2.36.2.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nThe supplied `parseChangedIntervals` recognizes only unquoted `+++ b/` headers. This call therefore omits the file's intervals. `verifyReview` then rejects its reviewed lines at Line 721.\n\nDecode Git's quoted pathnames before matching intervals, or explicitly classify these paths as unsupported before subject construction.","id":"0826879daa6c6b887d40240b4fec2a74bdf0feb22e15f102e998a5ef8415d4b2","intervals":[[680,680]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillAccounting.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve intervals for quoted Git pathnames."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"0eb076a29f2154938bc81d4cc9ba271e7d3d4ab0","body":"**Return exit code 1 for filesystem execution failures.**\n\nIf `readFile` or `atomicWrite` throws `EIO`, neither classifier recognizes the error. Both routes return exit code 3 instead of 1.\n\nKeep explicit operator refusals at 3. Classify filesystem execution failures at 1 so callers can distinguish execution failure from needs-human outcomes.\n\nAs per coding guidelines: “Exit codes: 0 clean, 1 thrown error, 2 arg error, 3 needs-human.”\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 301-307","id":"05097c9c0b6d81df90a40b06f2d6cf2d7170f431f4e07bbd5bca75bc11028eaa","intervals":[[172,172]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillSource.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Return exit code 1 for filesystem execution failures."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"10ae9d56596fcb63bf15b97e3ad04f55916e8932","body":"**Send empty input through `pipedGit`.**\n\nAt `src/adapters/crq/publishSource.ts`, Line 108 routes `{ input: new Uint8Array(0) }` through `execFile`. That branch never closes stdin. Thus, `git hash-object --stdin` waits for EOF until the 330-second timeout kills it, instead of returning the empty blob's object ID. Git reads this command's content from stdin; Node requires `stdin.end()` to finish that input. ([git-scm.com](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-hash-object?source=post_page---------------------------&utm_source=openai))\n\nCheck only `options?.input !== undefined`. The piped branch already calls `child.stdin.end(input)`, which also handles empty input.","id":"daf82f2030c989c4870b6a07e07bdd19f7f7d7fdecef305ef39c882a22f11853","intervals":[[108,108]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/publishSource.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Send empty input through `pipedGit`."}],"head":"d6cbcde051c83b0ee25f5067ceaabfc275a297af","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"17e075dd429f2875a912a0a6ee27271576d558a6","intervals":[[1,636]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/authorSnapshotInstall.ts"},{"blob":"97917f96b38ccc9113624d32ccd4108ad49a52c2","intervals":[[1,1343]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillAccounting.ts"},{"blob":"0eb076a29f2154938bc81d4cc9ba271e7d3d4ab0","intervals":[[1,310]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillSource.ts"},{"blob":"a1cab86734a3e0d1b886f3effa47b17f4722dcf6","intervals":[[1,430]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillSubjects.ts"},{"blob":"17bdc92125a6b015bbdb06daff2b4b5016bd29cc","intervals":[[1,398]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/coverageSource.ts"},{"blob":"10ae9d56596fcb63bf15b97e3ad04f55916e8932","intervals":[[1,371]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/publishSource.ts"},{"blob":"f36582c304ffe6b8f570d1abc3df21e7bbebb95f","intervals":[[1,448]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/reviewEffects.ts"},{"blob":"cd13cdf1a7ac37ab98bf40add57b7cabb038ee33","intervals":[[1,287]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/reviewVerify.ts"}],"job_id":"548e6c6410a06637861563a2d6eca21316446eb48bf232e4752dde224591095a:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"17e075dd429f2875a912a0a6ee27271576d558a6","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/authorSnapshotInstall.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"97917f96b38ccc9113624d32ccd4108ad49a52c2","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillAccounting.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"0eb076a29f2154938bc81d4cc9ba271e7d3d4ab0","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillSource.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","re